Most people in Washington thought that the Iranians would be keen to negotiate. And in the State Department, the working assumption was, probably this is all about money and we can do a deal, we can release frozen Iranian bank assets and that way we'll get the hostages back and this will take weeks, worst case months, but it's perfectly doable.

