00:45:57.000 --> 00:46:39.000
let's keep this on the front pages. That's mad. That's the worst strategy. I know. I know. It is a mad strategy. He said, I quote, it will provide a nice contrast between Carter and our friend from Massachusetts and how to handle a crisis. Oh, God. I mean, neither of them are very good in the crisis. That has to be said. No. So Carter takes this. whole of business incredibly seriously. He can't sleep. He's always going off to prayer meetings. He insists him personally meeting the families of all the hostages. His aides become quite worried about him. They say, you know, he's just constantly going on about the hostages, having all these meetings. And a lot of this, I think, is guilt. Because when he was asked by congressional leaders,

